{
  "schema": "s.puzzle2d.history-edit-runtime.v1",
  "description": "⏪️ Runtime acceptance of non-destructive history editing with puzzle 2d as the witness (ticket 26/09/30/NON-DESTRUCTIVE-HISTORY-EDITING design §4, §7, §16). One board, unless a scenario states its own; each scenario authors `log` (the leaves of its edits, oldest first; `row` addresses an edit and `mutation` a leaf inside a tool transaction's edit), edits it in a history session through the reserved `historyEdit*` verbs and checks the session, the per-mutation outcomes, the history-edit rows and the document head at each step. `heads` name documents: the board with `log` folded after replacing or dropping the leaves `edits` names, with the `edges` it holds and the `outcomes` that fold reports (log index, code, target); a step's `head` is the committed document and its `preview` the document a review paints; the Rust law (`🧪️tests/🧪️history-edit-runtime/🦀️.rs`) checks the app's head against them and against a fresh app folding that edited log, and the Python oracle (`🐍️.py` beside it) re-folds them independently with shapely and validates every leaf against its payload schema.",
  "board": {
    "schema": "board.ports.directed.v1",
    "nodes": [
      { "id": "left", "shape": "circle", "x": -200.0, "y": 0.0, "radius": 24.0, "text": "Left", "handles": [] },
      { "id": "mid", "shape": "circle", "x": 0.0, "y": 0.0, "radius": 24.0, "text": "Middle", "handles": [] },
      { "id": "pin", "shape": "circle", "x": 200.0, "y": 0.0, "radius": 24.0, "text": "Pin", "locked": true, "handles": [] }
    ],
    "edges": []
  },
  "scenarios": [
